                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's like Blackadder, but without the wit, and with too many double entendres, forsooth (also overused).\n\nApparently everyone in the late 16th century is either a fornicator or a murderer (or both). And the few who are neither, are droll.\n\nFor whatever historical accuracy/parody there is going on, it's over-shadowed by the devs' puerile writing, thinly veiled by latin and/or intellectual verbiage. I appreciate they're trying to insert modernity into 1592, but it all comes off feeling rather disgusting than amusing for the most part.\n\nThe idea was good, and execution is fairly well done, it's just severely dragged down by the incessant sexual overtones. I just can't personally recommend it.",
